From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gemini Mainline Experiment <gemini-mainline@example.invalid>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 14:01:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 112/112] soc: mediatek: add one-shot MT6797 WMT common
 initialization

Wi-Fi reception needs the WMT common initialization the vendor runs
after full-mode negotiation. Add it as one fixed table in the CONSYS
owner, in the selected vendor order for chip 0x0279: DLM power, MCU
clock raise, both ROM patches each followed by a WMT reset, MCU clock
restore, the LTE coexistence table, both PA rails around RF calibration,
and the board antenna mode.

The two ROM patches load through request_firmware and must match pinned
SHA-256 digests and the selected metadata before any command is sent.
Every exchange is checked against its expected event; the calibration
reply is captured rather than matched, because its success semantics
are not established. Each exchange has a 500 ms deadline, calibration
2 s, within a 30 s budget. The first failure stops the sequence and
keeps power, clocks and rails for reviewed recovery. Crystal trim,
co-clock, merged PCM and FM strap are not selected. No WLAN start or
scan follows.

Unsigned experiment draft; archive identity is non-certifying.
